                <pb facs="ec_d4-1" n="1" xml:id="ec_d4-1"/>

                <head>EC–4. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>During his trip to South America, April 27–May 15, 1958, Vice President Richard
                    M. Nixon visited Quito, May 9–11. A summary of his conversation with President
                    Camilo Ponce Enríquez of Ecuador on May 9 is printed as <ref target="#ec_d5"
                        >Document EC–5</ref>. Ecuadoran Minister of Economy Federico Intriago Arrata
                    presented a memorandum to Vice President Nixon containing Ecuadoran requests
                    with respect to pending economic matters. A copy of the 54-page memorandum was
                    enclosed with despatch 748 from Quito, May 20, 1958. (033.1100-NI/5–2058) In
                    despatch 732 from Quito, May 13, Ambassador Ravndal stated that Vice President
                    Nixon’s visit to Ecuador was an “unqualified success” and that it “did much to
                    cement good U.S.-Ecuadoran relations.” (722.00(W)/5–1358) For documentation on
                    Vice President Nixon’s visit to South America, see pages ff.</p>
            </div>
